History 
The railway between Uppsala and Lenna (old spelling of Länna) was opened in 1876 and was the first of all  railways in the region.

full_prefix:
Upsala-Lenna Jernväg

|}

Upsala-Lenna Järnväg (ULJ) (literally: Upsala-Lenna Railway, also nicknamed Lennakatten) is a narrow-gauge heritage railway in Uppsala County, Sweden. It is  long and is a part of the once extensive Roslagen network. The gauge is the , unique to Sweden.  The railway is run by the SRJmf society.

|}

